---
import Overlay from "../../templates/Overlay.astro";
import Content from "../../templates/Content.astro";
import Grid from "../../templates/Grid.astro";
import Card from "../../templates/Card.astro";
import Note from "../../templates/Note.astro";
---
<Overlay speaker="Finnbar McCloskey" logo>
    <Content>
        <h2>Use the pattern where it earns its keep</h2>
        <Grid columns={2}>
            <Card color="var(--color-kainos-green)">
                <h3>It helps when</h3>
                <p>Use cases have meaningful rules, persistence needs isolation, or multiple entry points share behavior.</p>
            </Card>
            <Card color="var(--color-kainos-grey)">
                <h3>Watch for</h3>
                <p>Pass-through layers, leaky database models, and abstractions that add indirection without flexibility.</p>
            </Card>
        </Grid>
        <Note>Start with the responsibility boundary. Add interfaces and extra layers only when they clarify a real change or test seam.</Note>
    </Content>
</Overlay>
